    "md5": "77fe16fa59b70f214d481c88c4d54524",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2006,
    "chunk_text": "Assetline Finance awarded ISO 14064 certification for Greenhouse Gas emissions verification\n\nAssetline Finance Limited (AFL), the financial services arm of the David Pieris Group, achieved a significant sustainability milestone by obtaining independent verification of its Greenhouse Gas (GHG) emissions inventory in accordance with ISO 14064-1:2018. The verification covers Scope 1, Scope 2, and Scope 3 emissions, including financed emissions. The certification was formally presented at a ceremony held at the Ministry of Environment, Battaramulla, on December 30, 2025.\n\nWhile upholding AFL\u2019s sustainability credentials at a national level, ISO 14064-1:2018 certification confirms that AFL\u2019s greenhouse gas emissions have been independently quantified and verified in accordance with internationally recognised standard for GHG accounting and reporting.\n\nThe verification covers Scope 1 \u2013 Direct emissions from owned and controlled sources, Scope 2 \u2013 Indirect emissions from purchased electricity and energy consumption and Scope 3 \u2013 Indirect emissions across the value chain, including employee commuting, waste disposal etc.\n\n\u201cThis milestone positions AFL as a forward-looking financial institution that proactively aligns its sustainability practices with the CBSL Roadmap and globally accepted standards. It also contributes meaningfully to Sri Lanka\u2019s transition towards a low-carbon and sustainable economy, supporting the nation\u2019s ambition to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2050.\u201d Says Ashan Nissanka Director and Chief Executive Officer of Assetline Finance.\n\nThe certificate was officially handed over by the Deputy Minister of Environment to AFL\u2019s Director and Chief Executive Officer, Ashan Nissanka, in the presence of senior government officials and other stakeholders. This achievement marks a significant milestone in AFL\u2019s sustainability journey and demonstrates strong alignment with the Central Bank of Sri Lanka\u2019s (CBSL) Roadmap for Sustainable Finance."
  },
