    "md5": "d6a3646867788acf347f0fb4f77dbd87",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "WindForce secures Letter of Award for 50 MW Mullikulam Wind Power Project \u2013 Lot 1\n\nFrom left: WindForce Chief Executive Officer Lasith Wimalasena, Director Hussain Akbarally, Managing Director\u00a0 Manjula Perera and CEB General Manager Eng.K.S.I. Kumara\n\nWindForce PLC has been awarded the official Letter of Award by the Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) for Lot 1 of the 50 MW Mullikulam Wind Power Project, confirming the company\u2019s position as the Lowest Cost Bidder for one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most strategically significant renewable energy developments.\n\nThe award follows the successful completion of all statutory and regulatory approvals, including clearance from the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee (CANC), the Cabinet of Ministers, and the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka (PUCSL)\u2014underscoring the robustness, transparency, and credibility of the national procurement process.\n\nLocated in the high-potential wind corridor of the Mannar region, the Mullikulam Wind Power Project will make a substantial contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s renewable energy capacity. The project directly supports national objectives to scale up clean energy generation, strengthen energy security, and reduce dependence on fossil-fuel-based power.\n\nThis milestone further strengthens WindForce\u2019s growing portfolio of utility-scale renewable energy assets and reinforces the company\u2019s leadership role in Sri Lanka\u2019s energy transition. WindForce remains firmly committed to delivering cost-competitive, reliable, and sustainable energy solutions, while upholding the highest standards of governance, regulatory compliance, environmental stewardship, and long-term stakeholder value creation.\n\nAs Sri Lanka accelerates its transition to a low-carbon energy future, landmark projects such as Mullikulam play a pivotal role in driving economic resilience, infrastructure development, and sustainable growth\u2014while reinforcing investor and public confidence in competitive, value-driven renewable energy procurement."
  },
